@startuml vista-desarrollo
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 240
title Vista de desarrollo (4+1)\nMódulos Maven, el frontend y el sentido de las dependencias.

package "piedrazul-system 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT" {
  package "piedrazul-backend" {
    component "shared-kernel" as SK
    component "user-module" as User
    component "availability-module" as Avail
    component "appointment-module" as Appt
    component "piedrazul-app" as App
  }
}

component "frontend" as Fe <<npm, Angular 21>>

User --> SK : Maven
Avail --> SK : Maven
Appt --> SK : Maven
App --> SK : Maven
App --> User : Maven
App --> Avail : Maven
App --> Appt : Maven
Fe ..> App : solo HTTP\nhttp://localhost:8080/api/v1\nsin dependencia de compilacion

note right of SK
  Sin Spring ni JPA.
  Puertos UserQueryPort y DoctorQueryPort,
  records UserSummary y DoctorSummary,
  DomainException.
end note

note bottom of User
  Dependencias extra: spring-boot-starter-data-jpa
  y spring-security-crypto.
end note

note bottom of Avail
  Dependencia extra: spring-boot-starter-data-jpa.
  No tiene pruebas.
end note

note bottom of Appt
  Dependencia extra: spring-boot-starter-data-jpa.
end note

note bottom of App
  Además: spring-boot-starter-web, postgresql,
  springdoc-openapi 2.5.0.
  Es el único módulo con main:
  PiedrazulApplication escanea com.groupsoft.piedrazul.
end note

@enduml

@startuml vista-desarrollo-hexagonal
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
title Vista de desarrollo — paquetes y límite hexagonal\nVerde: el dominio no conoce el adaptador. Ámbar: el dominio depende de Spring Data o JPA.

package "appointment-module" {
  package "appointment.domain.port" #CDECCB {
    interface AppointmentRepositoryPort
  }
  package "appointment.domain.model" #FDE8CD {
    class Appointment <<jakarta.persistence.Entity>>
    enum AppointmentStatus
  }
  package "appointment.application" #E7F0FA {
    class SearchAppointmentsByDoctorAndDateUseCase
    class AppointmentAssembler
    interface AppointmentResponseEnricher
    class ScheduleRules
  }
  package "appointment.infrastructure.persistence" #EEEEEE {
    class AppointmentRepositoryAdapter
    interface AppointmentJpaRepository <<JpaRepository>>
  }
}

SearchAppointmentsByDoctorAndDateUseCase --> AppointmentRepositoryPort
AppointmentRepositoryAdapter ..|> AppointmentRepositoryPort
AppointmentRepositoryAdapter --> AppointmentJpaRepository
AppointmentJpaRepository --> Appointment

note bottom of Appointment
  El caso de uso sí depende del puerto y no de JPA.
  La entidad, en cambio, está anotada con JPA
  dentro del paquete domain.model.
end note

package "user-module" {
  package "user.domain.repository" #FDE8CD {
    interface UserRepository <<JpaRepository>>
  }
  package "user.domain.model" #FDE8CD {
    class User <<jakarta.persistence.Entity>>
  }
  package "user.application" #E7F0FA {
    class LoginUseCase
    class RegisterUserUseCase
  }
  package "user.infrastructure.adapter" #EEEEEE {
    class UserQueryAdapter
  }
}

LoginUseCase --> UserRepository : sin puerto de salida
RegisterUserUseCase --> UserRepository : sin puerto de salida
UserQueryAdapter ..|> UserQueryPort
UserQueryAdapter --> UserRepository

note bottom of UserRepository
  El adaptador UserQueryAdapter cumple el puerto del shared-kernel
  para los otros módulos. Los casos de uso de login y registro
  no pasan por un puerto: conocen Spring Data.
end note

package "availability-module" {
  package "availability.domain.repository" #FDE8CD {
    interface DoctorRepository <<JpaRepository>>
  }
  package "availability.domain.model" #FDE8CD {
    class Doctor <<jakarta.persistence.Entity>>
  }
  package "availability.application.service" #E7F0FA {
    class DoctorQueryService
  }
  package "availability.infrastructure.adapter" #EEEEEE {
    class DoctorQueryAdapter
  }
}

DoctorQueryService --> DoctorRepository : sin puerto de salida
DoctorQueryAdapter ..|> DoctorQueryPort
DoctorQueryAdapter --> DoctorRepository

package "piedrazul-app.infrastructure" #F4F4F4 {
  class AuthController
  class AppointmentSearchController
  class DoctorController
  class AuthFilter
  class RegisterAccountService
}

AuthController --> LoginUseCase
AuthController --> RegisterAccountService
AppointmentSearchController --> SearchAppointmentsByDoctorAndDateUseCase
DoctorController --> DoctorQueryService
RegisterAccountService --> DoctorRepository : cruza al repositorio JPA
RegisterAccountService --> UserRepository : cruza al repositorio JPA

note as N
  Los módulos de negocio no se dependen entre sí por Maven.
  user, availability y appointment solo dependen de shared-kernel.
  Quien une los módulos es piedrazul-app.
  Esa unión a veces salta el puerto y usa el repositorio JPA del otro módulo.
end note

@enduml
